 Based upon this literature survey, the following conclusions can be drawn: (1) Most of the studies focus on specific parts of the process, e.g., water reduction and recycling, integrated energy supply using stillage and/or residual biomass, the use of co-generation systems (CHP (Combined heat and power), gasification, Rankine cycle); (2) Due to the energy-intensive nature of lignocellulosic ethanol production, different studies investigate improvements of the efficiency of ethanol production;
